- op: discuss  # 643b
  at: '2026-08-25T06:42:05Z'  # 643b
  by: agent  # 643b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 643b
  clock: 4  # 643b
  nonce: 643b  # 643b
  message: "SATISFIED 2026-08-25, PR #523, judged against this item's own repro and its own\nstatement. Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/campaign_p0_08252026/.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO, re-run at tip before the fix and after, with the control that\nmakes it readable printed in the same run:\n\n  BEFORE  repo owns myapp/os/ , calls os.path.join -> complete=True,  reason=''\n  CONTROL repo owns myapp/    , same call          -> complete=False, reason\n          names os.path\n  AFTER   both arms            -> complete=False, reason names os.path\n\nTHE FIX IS THE BOUND THIS ITEM ASKED FOR, with the two halves separated because\nthey answer different objections:\n  ONE STEP -- that is the length of a type name, which is the only thing\n    shortening exists to strip. A nested class (app.config.Loader.Inner) needs\n    two, is not licensed, and reports a gap: the safe direction.\n  NEVER TO A SINGLE COMPONENT -- a bare os / crypto / json / time is exactly\n    the spelling that collides with an ordinary directory name, and `analyzed`\n    is matched as a component-bounded INFIX (it must be, to tolerate packaging\n    prefixes), which makes a one-component needle match almost anywhere.\n\nWHAT I TRIED FIRST AND WHY IT IS WRONG, recorded so nobody re-proposes it:\n\"match the WHOLE spelling as an infix but the SHORTENED one as a SUFFIX\". That\nlooks tighter and is refuted by INV-liloh's own shipped fixture --\nhypergumbo_core.scip._generated shortens to hypergumbo_core.scip, which sits\nINSIDE packages.hypergumbo-core.src.hypergumbo_core.scip.loader and is not a\nsuffix of it. The suffix rule would have re-broken INV-liloh.\n\nA/B OVER FIVE REAL REPO-LANGUAGE PAIRS. Both arms run in ONE process over ONE\nedge population, which is legitimate here because the predicate is pure -- arm\nA is the old unbounded loop reimplemented verbatim, arm B is the shipped\nfunction. A hard assertion in the probe says the bound can only ever REFUSE\n(arm B never vouched where arm A did not); it held on every repo.\n\n  caddy/go           0 change            -- the separator-fold path already covered it\n  hypergumbo/python  14 -> 7 vouched     -- 7 newly disclosed\n  clover/java        754 -> 250 vouched  -- 504 newly disclosed\n  Alamofire/rust     no population\n  caddy/python       no population\n\nBOTH NON-ZERO RESULTS ARE REAL THIRD-PARTY CODE READING AS FIRST-PARTY:\n  starlette is a DECLARED DEPENDENCY (starlette>=1.3.1 in\n    hypergumbo-tracker/pyproject.toml), vouched for by a TEST FIXTURE directory\n    at packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/fixtures/route-parity/starlette -- on\n    hypergumbo's OWN self-claims. All 7 newly disclosed entries are starlette.*.\n  clover's 504 are SHADED dependencies -- clover.antlr.*,\n    clover.com.google.common.* (guava), clover.com.lowagie.text.* (iText) --\n    vouched for by the `clover` component in the repo's own\n    com.atlassian.clover package path.\n\nRELATIONSHIP TO INV-juvul, since they are the same shape one layer apart.\nINV-juvul found that folding os/exec to os.exec and THEN shortening suppressed\nthe subprocess module because caddy owns internal/filesystems/os.go, and fixed\nit by testing the FOLDED spelling whole. The dotted loop was left unbounded and\nis what this item found. The function's docstring still said \"Tests every\ndotted prefix\"; it is rewritten rather than annotated."  # 643b
